From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:18:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2835_fbd: 16 bpp is RGB565 with red high, also under
 fbswap

The 16 bpp case under fbswap put red in the low bits, by analogy with
the 24 bpp case, and was marked unverified on hardware. On a Raspberry
Pi 500+ the HVS scans this framebuffer out as HVS_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGB565
with pixel order XRGB (DRM_FORMAT_RGB565, red in bits 15:11), and
U-Boot's EFI GOP packs it the same way. With red low, everything the
kernel drew there had red and blue swapped: the console's colours and
NextBSD's boot splash, whose cube came out brown instead of blue-grey
right after the loader had drawn it correctly.

Part of nextbsd/nextbsd#542 (nextbsd-kernel#433).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c | 13 ++++++-------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c b/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c
index dfcb587fc..6a7ab3188 100644
--- a/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c
+++ b/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c
@@ -229,15 +229,14 @@ bcm_fb_setup_fbd(struct bcmsc_softc *sc)
 			/*
 			 * RGB565. Reached when the firmware would not restructure
 			 * the framebuffer and we fell back to the depth its
-			 * stride implies. Channel order is the one the 24bpp case
-			 * below uses -- red in the low bits under fbswap -- and is
-			 * unverified on hardware: if red and blue come out
-			 * swapped, exchange the two 0x1f entries. Geometry is
-			 * correct either way, so the console is readable
-			 * regardless.
+			 * stride implies. Red is in the high bits even under
+			 * fbswap: measured on a Raspberry Pi 500+, the HVS scans
+			 * this buffer out as HVS_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGB565 with pixel
+			 * order XRGB (DRM_FORMAT_RGB565), and U-Boot's GOP packs
+			 * it the same way.
 			 */
 			vt_config_cons_colors(&sc->info,
-			    COLOR_FORMAT_RGB, 0x1f, 0, 0x3f, 5, 0x1f, 11);
+			    COLOR_FORMAT_RGB, 0x1f, 11, 0x3f, 5, 0x1f, 0);
 			sc->info.fb_cmsize = 16;
 			break;
 		case 24:
